\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,132.9 52,132.9 55.1,132.9 58.1,132.9 61.1,132.8 64.1,132.8 67.2,132.8 70.2,132.8 73.2,132.8 76.2,132.7 79.2,132.7 82.3,132.6 85.3,132.6 88.3,132.5 91.3,132.4 94.4,132.3 97.4,132.2 100.4,132.1 103.4,132 106.4,131.8 109.5,131.7 112.5,131.5 115.5,131.3 118.5,131.1 121.6,130.9 124.6,130.6 127.6,130.3 130.6,130 133.6,129.7 136.7,129.4 139.7,129 142.7,128.6 145.7,128.2 148.8,127.8 151.8,127.3 154.8,126.9 157.8,126.3 160.8,125.8 163.9,125.2 166.9,124.6 169.9,124 172.9,123.3 176,122.6 179,121.9 182,121.1 185,120.3 188,119.5 191.1,118.6 194.1,117.7 197.1,116.8 200.1,115.8 203.2,114.8 206.2,113.7 209.2,112.6 212.2,111.4 215.2,110.3 218.3,109 221.3,107.7 224.3,106.4 227.3,105.1 230.4,103.6 233.4,102.2 236.4,100.7 239.4,99.1 242.4,97.5 245.5,95.9 248.5,94.1 251.5,92.4 254.5,90.6 257.6,88.7 260.6,86.8 263.6,84.8 266.6,82.8 269.6,80.7 272.7,78.6 275.7,76.4 278.7,74.1 281.7,71.8 284.8,69.4 287.8,67 290.8,64.4 293.8,61.9 296.8,59.3 299.9,56.6 302.9,53.8 305.9,51 308.9,48.1 312,45.1 315,42.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that bends as its input grows.","steps":["Name the chosen point and the step away from it.","Evaluate the function at the chosen point, and evaluate the derivative at that same point.","Add the derivative just computed times the step to the function value just computed."]},{"id":"local-linear-approximation-r2-q1","version":1,"round":2,"type":"symbolic","prompt":"The value at a chosen point \\(a\\) is \\(p\\), and the derivative there is \\(m\\). Write the linear approximation at a new point \\(x\\), in the names p, m, a, and x.","answer":"p+m*(x-a)","tolerance":0.001,"explanation":"The approximation is the value \\(p\\) plus the slope \\(m\\) times the step \\(x - a\\). Leaving out \\(p\\) reports only the change. Using \\(x\\) in place of the step treats the new coordinate as if the chosen point were zero. Swapping \\(p\\) and \\(m\\) mixes a value with a slope.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>A smooth curve</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,132.9 52,132.9 55.1,132.9 58.1,132.9 61.1,132.8 64.1,132.8 67.2,132.8 70.2,132.8 73.2,132.8 76.2,132.7 79.2,132.7 82.3,132.6 85.3,132.6 88.3,132.5 91.3,132.4 94.4,132.3 97.4,132.2 100.4,132.1 103.4,132 106.4,131.8 109.5,131.7 112.5,131.5 115.5,131.3 118.5,131.1 121.6,130.9 124.6,130.6 127.6,130.3 130.6,130 133.6,129.7 136.7,129.4 139.7,129 142.7,128.6 145.7,128.2 148.8,127.8 151.8,127.3 154.8,126.9 157.8,126.3 160.8,125.8 163.9,125.2 166.9,124.6 169.9,124 172.9,123.3 176,122.6 179,121.9 182,121.1 185,120.3 188,119.5 191.1,118.6 194.1,117.7 197.1,116.8 200.1,115.8 203.2,114.8 206.2,113.7 209.2,112.6 212.2,111.4 215.2,110.3 218.3,109 221.3,107.7 224.3,106.4 227.3,105.1 230.4,103.6 233.4,102.2 236.4,100.7 239.4,99.1 242.4,97.5 245.5,95.9 248.5,94.1 251.5,92.4 254.5,90.6 257.6,88.7 260.6,86.8 263.6,84.8 266.6,82.8 269.6,80.7 272.7,78.6 275.7,76.4 278.7,74.1 281.7,71.8 284.8,69.4 287.8,67 290.8,64.4 293.8,61.9 296.8,59.3 299.9,56.6 302.9,53.8 305.9,51 308.9,48.1 312,45.1 315,42.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that bends as its input grows.","variables":[{"name":"p","min":1.0,"max":6.0},{"name":"m","min":-3.0,"max":3.0},{"name":"a","min":0.5,"max":2.0},{"name":"x","min":0.2,"max":4.0}],"alternates":["m*(x-a)+p","p+(x-a)*m"]},{"id":"local-linear-approximation-r2-q2","version":1,"round":2,"type":"numeric","prompt":"Let \\(f(x) = 1/x\\). At \\(x = 4\\), a step of \\(+0.5\\) is proposed. What change does the linear approximation predict?","answer":-0.03125,"unit":"","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"The derivative of \\(1/x\\) is \\(-1/x^2\\), so at \\(x = 4\\) the slope is \\(-1/16\\). The predicted change is that slope times \\(0.5\\), which is \\(-0.03125\\). The new value of the function is a different question. The slope at \\(4.5\\), or the ratio \\(1/4\\), is not the change predicted from the chosen point.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>A smooth curve</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,132.9 52,132.9 55.1,132.9 58.1,132.9 61.1,132.8 64.1,132.8 67.2,132.8 70.2,132.8 73.2,132.8 76.2,132.7 79.2,132.7 82.3,132.6 85.3,132.6 88.3,132.5 91.3,132.4 94.4,132.3 97.4,132.2 100.4,132.1 103.4,132 106.4,131.8 109.5,131.7 11