hat product to the value at \\(a\\)."],"flaw_index":2,"reasons":["The derivative belongs at the chosen point, not at the new point.","The function value at the chosen point should be left out.","The step should be added to the slope instead of multiplied."],"correct_reason":0},{"id":"local-linear-approximation-r3-q2","version":1,"round":3,"type":"numeric","prompt":"Let \\(f(x) = x^2 + 3x\\). What is the derivative at \\(x = 1\\), the slope the linear approximation uses there?","answer":5.0,"unit":"","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"The derivative is \\(2x + 3\\). At \\(x = 1\\) that is \\(5\\). The function value \\(4\\) is the constant term of the approximation, not the slope. The derivative at a different point, or the ratio \\(f(1)/1 = 4\\), does not multiply the step.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>A smooth curve</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,132.9 52,132.9 55.1,132.9 58.1,132.9 61.1,132.8 64.1,132.8 67.2,132.8 70.2,132.8 73.2,132.8 76.2,132.7 79.2,132.7 82.3,132.6 85.3,132.6 88.3,132.5 91.3,132.4 94.4,132.3 97.4,132.2 100.4,132.1 103.4,132 106.4,131.8 109.5,131.7 112.5,131.5 115.5,131.3 118.5,131.1 121.6,130.9 124.6,130.6 127.6,130.3 130.6,130 133.6,129.7 136.7,129.4 139.7,129 142.7,128.6 145.7,128.2 148.8,127.8 151.8,127.3 154.8,126.9 157.8,126.3 160.8,125.8 163.9,125.2 166.9,124.6 169.9,