=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,132.9 52,132.9 55.1,132.9 58.1,132.9 61.1,132.8 64.1,132.8 67.2,132.8 70.2,132.8 73.2,132.8 76.2,132.7 79.2,132.7 82.3,132.6 85.3,132.6 88.3,132.5 91.3,132.4 94.4,132.3 97.4,132.2 100.4,132.1 103.4,132 106.4,131.8 109.5,131.7 112.5,131.5 115.5,131.3 118.5,131.1 121.6,130.9 124.6,130.6 127.6,130.3 130.6,130 133.6,129.7 136.7,129.4 139.7,129 142.7,128.6 145.7,128.2 148.8,127.8 151.8,127.3 154.8,126.9 157.8,126.3 160.8,125.8 163.9,125.2 166.9,124.6 169.9,124 172.9,123.3 176,122.6 179,121.9 182,121.1 185,120.3 188,119.5 191.1,118.6 194.1,117.7 197.1,116.8 200.1,115.8 203.2,114.8 206.2,113.7 209.2,112.6 212.2,111.4 215.2,110.3 218.3,109 221.3,107.7 224.3,106.4 227.3,105.1 230.4,103.6 233.4,102.2 236.4,100.7 239.4,99.1 242.4,97.5 245.5,95.9 248.5,94.1 251.5,92.4 254.5,90.6 257.6,88.7 260.6,86.8 263.6,84.8 266.6,82.8 269.6,80.7 272.7,78.6 275.7,76.4 278.7,74.1 281.7,71.8 284.8,69.4 287.8,67 290.8,64.4 293.8,61.9 296.8,59.3 299.9,56.6 302.9,53.8 305.9,51 308.9,48.1 312,45.1 315,42.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that bends as its input grows."},{"id":"local-linear-approximation-r4-q2","version":1,"round":4,"type":"mc","prompt":"The same replacement, applied to a rate that depends on a state and an input, is stored as two partial derivatives. Those partial derivatives are evaluated","options":["at a convenient point that is not the resting condition","only with respect to time, after the rate has been integrated","at the resting condition, once in the state and once in the input","after the rate is replaced by its second derivative"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"A later skill names the state partial \\(A\\) and the input partial \\(B\\), both evaluated where the rate is zero. A point that is not resting is a different expansion. Time is not one of those two variables. The second derivative is a later correction, not these two first partials.","preview":["linearization"],"figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 130\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>Two partial-derivative blocks</title><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"28\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">[</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"28\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">]</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">A   B</text></svg>","figure_alt":"Two blocks side by side, one for each partial derivative."},{"id":"local-linear-approximation-r4-q3","version":2,"round":4,"type":"multi","prompt":"Which statements about the error of the linear approximation are true?","options":["The error is what is left after the value and the first derivative at the chosen point are matched.","For a smooth function, the error is of higher order than the step.","The second derivative has to be matched before this first-order formula can be written.","The error is zero for every cubic, at every step."],"explanation":"The error is the remainder after the value and the first derivative at the chosen point are matched, and that remainder is higher order in the step. The second derivative is an extra term a later skill adds. It is not required before the linear formula exists. A cubic still has a nonzero error at a finite step.","preview":["taylor-approximation-multivariable"],"figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>A smooth curve</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">x</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,132.9 52,132.9 55.1,132.9 58.1,132.9 61.1,132.8 64.1,132.8 67.2,132.8 70.2,132.8 73.2,132.8 76.2,132.7 79.2,132.7 82.3,132.6 85.3,132.6 88.3,132.5 91.3,132.4 94.4,132.3 97.4,132.2 100.4,132.1 103.4,132 106.4,131.8 109.5,131.7 112.5,131.5 115.5,131.3 118.5,131.1 121.6,130.9 124.6,130.6 127.6,130.3 130.6,130 133.6,129.7 136.7,129.4 139.7,129 142.7,128.6 145.7,128.2 148.8,127.8 151.8,127.3 154.8,126.9 157.8,126.3 160.8,125.8 163.9,125.2 166.9,124.6 169.9,124 172.9,123.3 176,122.6 179,121.9 182,121.1 185,120.3 188,119.5 191.1,118.6 194.1,117.7 197.1,116.8 200.1,115.8 203.2,114.8 206.2,113.7 209.2,112.6 212.2,111.4 215.2,110.3 218.3,109 221.3,107.7 224.3,106.4 227.3,105.1 230.4,103.6 233.4,102.2 236.4,100.7 239.4,99.1 242.4,97.5 245.5,95.9 248.5,94.1 251.5,92.4 254.5,90.6 257.6,88.7 260.6,86.8 263.6,84.8 266.6,82.8 269.6,80.7 272.7,78.6 275.7,76.4 278.7,74.1 281.7,71.8 284.8,69.4 287.8,67 290.8,64.4 293.8,61.9 296.8,59.3 299.9,56.6 302.9,53.8 305.9,51 308.9,48.1 312,45.1 315,42.1 318,39\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A smooth curve that bends as its input grows.","correct_indices":[0,1]}]}